WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
Take a dose of medicine, and its
level in your blood starts to fall.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.010
After a few hours, the level has halved.

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.790
After a few more, it has halved again.

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.730
Start with a big dose or a small one,
and the halving time stays the same.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.470
Why does a medicine's level in
the blood halve every few hours,

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.370
however high it starts?

7
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.250
In this mission, you'll read
concentration–time graphs for zero-,

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.770
first- and second-order reactions.

9
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.330
You'll read rate–concentration graphs too,

10
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.570
and learn not to confuse
the two kinds of graph.

11
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:37.960
Your mission: explain why the medicine's
level always takes the same time to halve.
